# Pairs with EventualConvergence in ReplicationCausalDelivery. Option B for
# #4464: a parked entry is not acknowledged until it can be applied, and a
# re-delivery of a buffered entry is deferred too. The shipper backs off and
# re-ships the same entry, so its whole line stalls behind it. With shipping
# order free to differ from authoring order, b ships b2 (depending on a1)
# ahead of b1 and a ships a2 (depending on b1) ahead of a1: each stalled head
# holds back the other's dependency, and the receiver never converges.
# Fairness is unchanged: this is a protocol defect, not a starved action.
MODULE: EventualConvergenceDeferredParkStalls
TARGET: EventualConvergence
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: withholding the ack for a parked entry stalls its shipper, and a cross-origin dependency cycle deadlocks the receiver
PERTURBS: Deliver
DEADLOCK: off

--- FIND
       /\ \/ /\ w \in applied \cup buf
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a buffered entry's re-delivery is deferred, not acknowledged.
       /\ \/ /\ w \in applied
--- END

--- FIND
             /\ wake' = TRUE
             /\ cursor' = [cursor EXCEPT ![s] = i]
--- REPLACE
             /\ wake' = TRUE
\* MUTATION: the parked entry is not acknowledged; the shipper stalls on it.
             /\ UNCHANGED cursor
--- END
